A||N||3||maninblack||87 se v6 5sp rear calipers||||8||
Z||000000||maninblack||09-08-2000||09:40 PM||||does anyone have any information on the rear calipers on 87 5sp v6 se?.I am trying to put<BR>the cross-drilled rotors and upgrades pads from the fiero store on the rear but the <BR>"center" bit the stick out from the caliper<BR>would not adjust.I tried to push it in or screw it back for spacing with out luck.Does any one know if I need special tool to readjust the high of that center piece?<BR>thx||||reg||8
Z||000001||theogre||09-08-2000||10:49 PM||||Take off the E brake arm.<P>Put a large socket over the "bolt"  the e brake arm was attached to. Make sure the socket completely clears the e brake bolt.<P>Press the piston in with a big C clamp. (The E brake actuator will rotate under the socket.)||||reg||1
Z||000002||maninblack||09-09-2000||08:33 AM||||thank you very much<BR>I give that a try today||||reg||14
Z||000003||maninblack||09-09-2000||10:06 PM||||theogre: everything is done now,the only glitch are the rotors which is sligthly<BR>thicker than the stock one,but it still fit properly.Now I am going to look for some hubcentric wheels for my car.<BR>thx for the info<BR>case close  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||6
